note flint-manifest: bounded reader for the pinned Flint BF16 checkpoint (aien-architecture-mv#353,
note Core #802 P0). Usage: flint-manifest CONFIG INDEX SHARD_DIR [TOKDIR]. It admits config.json,
note model.safetensors.index.json and every safetensors header named by the index, and refuses
note anything outside the pinned layout. On success stdout is the tensor inventory TSV (one row per
note tensor: name, shard, dtype, shape, begin, end; shards in name order, rows in header order) and
note stderr carries one summary line. With TOKDIR, stdout is instead the load report (file, tokenizer
note and inventory sha256, control tokens, per-shard header identity, per-class tensor counts,
note parameters and bytes, reconciled totals). On refusal nothing is written to stdout, stderr
note carries "refused N reason" and the exit status is N (table in om/flint/README.md).
note Compose: { printf 'om2\n'; cat om/vendor/json.om om/vendor/sha256.om om/flint/manifest.om; } | omc
note Canonical tensor id (slot): 0 embed, 1 final norm, 2 lm_head, then 3 + layer * 784 + kind.
note Kinds 0..8 every layer, 9..11 dense MLP (layers 0 and 1), 12..15 router and shared expert,
note 16 + 3 * expert + j routed expert projections (j 0 gate, 1 up, 2 down), MoE layers 2..48.

const FMX ulong 99999
const FMNS ulong 38419
const FBOS ulong 150000
const FPAD ulong 150001
global ga uchar 16384
global gas ulong 8
global gal ulong 8
global gpth uchar 4352
global gx uchar 4194304
global gsn uchar 8192
global gsl ulong 64
global gord ulong 64
global gix uchar 38419
global gsee uchar 38419
global gbg ulong 4096
global gen ulong 4096
global gst ulong 32
global gstb uchar 128
global gh8 uchar 8
global geb uchar 512
global gdg uchar 24
global gob uchar 8388608
global gsb ulong 38419
global glx ulong 256
global gxc ulong 64
global gkc ulong 24
global gkp ulong 24
global gkb ulong 24
global ghs uchar 4352
global gsz ulong 64
global ghl ulong 64
global gsc ulong 64

note gst: 0 index tensors, 1 total_size, 2 params, 3 routed params, 4 tensor bytes, 5 stdout fill,
note 6 header tensors, 7 index cursor, 8 index length, 9 last fstat size, 10 shard index,
note 11 shard data length, 12 shard entries, 13 shard count, 14 stderr fill, 15 string start,
note 16 string length, 17 number end, 18 mantissa, 19 biased exponent, 20 mantissa end,
note 21 report mode (TOKDIR given), 22 config bytes.
note gsb: slot -> data begin; glx: experts in name order; gxc: per-shard cursor of the layout walk;
note gkc/gkp/gkb: per report class tensors, parameters, bytes; ghs: 64 hex sha256 per shard
note header, then slot 64 config, 65 index, 66 inventory TSV, 67 last TOKDIR file;
note gsz/ghl/gsc: per shard file bytes, header bytes, tensors.

